AB  - In worldwide, inadequate safety measures and reckless driving are common causes of bike accidents, resulting in injuries and fatalities. Internet of Things (IoT) technology in the field of safety has gained significant attention. This paper proposes the implementation of a smart helmet with cooling system using IOT technology equipped with sensors and communication modules which include a range of features such as cooling system, accident detection, GPS tracking, and display essential parameters such as alcohol level and temperature value. The smart helmet is designed with multiple objectives aimed at improving rider safety and encouraging responsible driving. Firstly, it incorporates a cooling system using Peltier to ensure the rider’s comfort, especially during long journeys. Additionally, the helmet features a display that shows crucial parameters like alcohol level and temperature. Furthermore, it includes an anti-theft mechanism to safeguard the helmet from unauthorized access, this is achieved by equipping a real-time tracking system that can be accessed through a dedicated app or website. This allows for monitoring sensor values and tracking data, enhancing overall safety measures for the rider. Hardware implementation of the proposed system is successfully done and tested for different users.
ER  - 

