AB  - The "HelmetGuard" program is a groundbreaking development in the realm of safety gear since it integrates Internet of Things (IoT) technology into conventional helmets. This method aims to modernize the traditional helmet and provide a safer, smarter, and more interactive headgear. The HelmetGuard collects real-time information on the user’s surroundings and vital signs via integrated sensors, wireless communication modules, and a central processing unit. This information is then processed and evaluated to deliver immediate feedback, allowing preventative safety steps. The helmet has functions including sleep detection, GPS tracking, alcohol detection, ignition control, and required mandatory presence of helmet. It also has features like ignition control and accident detection. The HelmetGuard seeks to greatly improve user safety and make the world a safer place by seamlessly integrating IoT capabilities with safety equipment.
ER  - 

