AB  - The proliferation of urbanization, population, and transportation infrastructure has led to an increase in the number of vehicles on the roads, leading to higher accident rates. This paper endeavors with implementing a real-time based vehicular control system with smart alcohol, seat-belt, speed, collision detection and avoidance system. The system has undergone extensive training to distinguish high-risk and low-risk scenarios by incorporating Support Vector Machines with radial basis function to classify and manage potential accidents with a remarkable accuracy rate of 95.8%. If any accident occurs the system is capable of tracking and reporting the accident and its location to the nearest police station with the help of GSM and GPS module. This research integrates advanced technologies and machine learning algorithms to develop a highly efficient and reliable vehicular control system, contributing to the advancement of the field.
ER  - 

