AB  - A vehicle security system with multiple functions employs ESP32, incorporating several sensors for tasks including high beam detection, accident identification, object detection, one-handed feature inspections, alcohol level monitoring, and locating the vehicle. The system uses sophisticated detection technologies, voice alerts, notifications, and real-time GPS location monitoring. tracking to boost vehicle safety and maintain driver vigilance. when headlights from approaching vehicles are sensed, the system instantly reduces the brightness of the car's headlights to enhance safety. In the event of an accident, the tilt sensor sends alerts to contacts provides precise location information to facilitate a prompt response. Ultrasonic sensors continuously measures the distances to nearby objects, thereby improving situational awareness and reducing the risk of collisions. In addition, an IR sensor is employed to detect identify the presence of one-handed features, and in the event that such features are detected, the IR sensor triggers an audible warning to The driver. This advanced vehicle protection system is designed not only to enhance driver safety and security but also to promote a proactive driving strategy by providing time, tracking, notifications, and assistance.
ER  - 

