AB  - The issue of dust and smoke resulting from forest fires in northern Thailand. This is caused by people burning the forest to get forest products. Individuals can start forest fires by intentionally burning the forest to extract forest resources. Deforestation negatively affects the well-being of vulnerable patients and has repercussions on public health. The decrease in tourist numbers impacts the economy. Individuals setting fire to the forest to gather forest resources impact government and public sector connections. The education sector has implemented many strategies to educate and mitigate forest fires. There is a fire suppression system. Remove garbage, leaves, and branches that are flammable. However, forest fires remain a concern. Collaboration among three entities in the community can aid in preventing unauthorized forest fires through communal procedures. From multiple ministries, the local organization department, and the central government Collaborating to safeguard Forest fire suppression and afforestation This study is a component of the forest fire surveillance division. If the forest fire's location is not clearly indicated, participating in combined operations will lead to issues because of the overlap in operational responsibilities. Previously, thermal imaging satellites were utilized for coordinate determination. If the satellite completes two orbits each day and identifies a hot location, it initiates a forest fire. Firefighters cannot reach the area to put out forest fires; thus, they need to enter from a nearby, accessible location. Joining the forest fire prevention volunteer organization is challenging and will require approximately 24 to 25 hours. This study aims to conserve energy by utilizing an loT system that transmits peer-to-peer signals. Individuals are prepared to dismantle this system. The villagers can develop it themselves due to its modest cost of $10. During a forest fire (temperature exceeding 50 degrees Celsius), specific operational methods are employed. The temperature-sensing system activates the microcontroller from its dormant condition. Revert to low-power mode and adjust the operating parameters to normal to transmit data signals. The range of peer-to-peer transmission is influenced by the plant density per square meter the air temperature and humidity in forest regions prone to frequent fires. The transmission range will be 100 meters between places with strong RSSI values. The last alarm point will be positioned close to the WiFi hot-spot to transmit the signal to the internet system for processing and distribution. Alerting Line application of wildfire GPS location. The system can detect heat and transmit a signal in under 3 minutes during testing. (Abstract)
ER  - 

