AB  - The creation of a sophisticated two-wheeler helmet in India seeks to drastically lower the amount of traffic accidents brought on by careless and inebriated driving. It is critical to solve this issue since, according to data, two-wheelers are involved in around 25% of traffic incidents in India. Enormous number of sensors have been incorporated into the construction of the smart helmet. First of all, alcohol sensors are built in to determine whether a cyclist has drunk before riding. This function can serve as a preventative measure by discouraging people from driving when intoxicated, hence lowering the possibility of accidents brought on by poor judgment. Additionally, a rider's helmet is continually monitored by an infrared sensor. Additionally, the helmet has a vibration detector attached to detect harsh impacts during accidents. This sensor will send an alarm to emergency services or predetermined contacts in the case of a collision, enabling prompt aid and potentially life-saving treatments. The two-wheeler's whereabouts may be tracked in real-time thanks to the GPS capability. The GPS on the helmet can determine the rider's location in the event of an accident, assisting first responders in quickly reaching the scene even in outlying or unfamiliar locations. The ingenious helmet attempts to make two-wheeler riders in India safer by integrating these cutting-edge sensors. The entire system can provide fast aid in times of need in addition to preventing accidents brought on by intoxicated, careless, or fatigued driving. This program might potentially save many lives and encourage safe driving habits, which would ultimately lead to a decline in traffic accidents and their severe effects.
ER  - 

