AB  - This research work presents an Advanced Vehicle Safety and Monitoring System designed to enhance driver safety, record vehicle conditions, and provide real-time alerts during emergencies. The system integrates various sensors and communication modules to ensure a comprehensive monitoring solution. An alcohol sensor detects impaired driving, while the MEMS sensor identifies any abnormal tilting or movement of the vehicle. Ultrasonic sensors are employed to monitor nearby obstacles, and a potentiometer is used for speed monitoring. The GPS and GSM modules work together to provide real-time location updates and send alerts in case of abnormal situations. The APR9600 voice module delivers audio warnings for critical conditions, while an LCD screen displays key information such as speed and location. A push-button switch offers an emergency alert feature, allowing drivers to quickly signal distress. Additionally, a buzzer and speaker are incorporated to provide audible alerts. This system, powered by an ESP32 microcontroller, ensures timely emergency responses, improves overall vehicle safety, and aids in accident analysis for better decision-making.
