AB  - In today’s changing world, the rise in car accidents and deaths on the road is an outcome of increasing traffic and population growth. The World Health Organization (WHO) states that a concerning 1.35 million lives are lost each year due to road accidents with factors like alcohol use, reckless driving and speeding playing roles. To make matters worse a significant 55 percent of road fatalities remain unreported leading to delays in emergency responses and sadly more deaths. To solve this issue, an effective solution emerges through the merging of the Internet of Things (IoT) and blockchain technologies. The proposed system for warning about car collisions combines an Arduino controller with sensors such as accelerometers and vibration sensors. These sensors quickly identify dangers activating the emergency system that uses GPS to pinpoint locations and a GSM module to communicate with emergency services. Immediate alerts are then sent out to designated contacts for help. By incorporating technology into the mix, the efficiency of emergency alerts is further boosted by ensuring communication between vehicles and medical facilities. This integration promotes trust and transparency through encrypted data sharing and verification methods thereby enhancing the reliability of the system. This novel approach significantly reduces fatalities by creating a transparent environment, for emergency assistance. Moreover, the system’s cost and easy availability make it suitable for use in all types of vehicles irrespective of their brand or design. Choosing this budget option has promise not just in lowering the number of deaths but also, in improving overall road safety worldwide.
ER  - 

